@startuml 01g-activity-flash-personalize
!include ../_style.iuml
title Pi-Gen imaging: flash and personalize one SD card (scripts/personalize-node.sh, macOS)

start
:Flash pi-gen/deploy/*-ivalice.img to the SD card
(manual: Raspberry Pi Imager, balenaEtcher or dd);
note right
  No flash script exists in the repo. CM4 Lite
  boots from SD, so usbboot/rpiboot (present in
  cmCluster/usbboot) is only needed for eMMC CM4s.
end note
:Re-insert card, macOS mounts the FAT partition as "bootfs";
:./scripts/personalize-node.sh [args] [~--with-k3s] [~--force];
if (~--list?) then (yes)
  :print [done]/[pending] per host from .last-personalize;
  stop
endif
if (0 positional args? (auto)) then (yes)
  :next host in order dalmasca, archadia, rozarria,
  bhujerba, nabradia, kerwon not in .last-personalize;
  :needs a TTY, prompt "Proceed? [y/N]";
elseif (1-2 args? (shortcut)) then (yes)
  :hostname [disk], role and IP from HOST_IPS table;
elseif (3-4 args? (legacy)) then (yes)
  :role host ip/cidr [disk], validated against
  HOST_IPS unless ~--force;
else (other)
  :usage, exit 2;
  stop
endif
if (uname is Darwin?) then (no)
  :ERROR macOS only (diskutil);
  stop
endif
:find mount point (diskutil info bootfs, or <disk>s1);
:compose ivalice-node.conf
NODE_ROLE, NODE_HOSTNAME, NODE_IP (CIDR), NODE_K3S=yes|no;
if (existing conf on card?) then (yes)
  if (same NODE_* values?) then (yes)
    :"[ok] unchanged", eject;
    stop
  elseif (~--force?) then (no)
    :ERROR refuse to overwrite;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
endif
if (role head and a head was written to a different disk < 24 h ago?) then (yes)
  :WARNING two heads would fight for 10.42.0.1;
endif
:write /Volumes/bootfs/ivalice-node.conf;
:append role|host|ip|disk|timestamp to .last-personalize;
:diskutil eject;
stop

note right #FFE4E1
  FINDING 1: README quick start calls
  "~--hostname X ~--ip Y ~--role Z". The script
  has no such flags: 6 positionals hit the
  usage branch. Use "personalize-node.sh X".
  FINDING 2: "declare -A" needs bash 4+;
  macOS /bin/bash is 3.2, so this needs
  Homebrew bash first on PATH.
end note
@enduml
